# planegcs, as delivered

This directory is a build of planegcs from FreeCAD @TAG@ and everything the
licence obliges the sender to hand over with it. `tools/build-planegcs.sh`
filled the version, digest, platform and compiler in when the build was made,
so what you are reading describes this build and not a general case.

## What is here

| Path | What it is | Licence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `@LIBRARY@` | the planegcs shared library, built for @PLATFORM@ | LGPL-2.0-or-later |
| `@IMPORT_LIBRARY@` | linker metadata for the library above, on Windows only, where it is what a relink reads. It carries no planegcs implementation | LGPL-2.0-or-later |
| `tree/App/planegcs/` | the complete corresponding source, byte-identical to the release | LGPL-2.0-or-later |
| `tree/boost_graph_adjacency_list.hpp` | from the same release, byte-identical | LGPL-2.0-or-later |
| `LICENSE-FreeCAD-LGPL-2.0-or-later.txt` | the full licence text, from the same release | |
| `tree/SketcherGlobal.h`, `tree/FCConfig.h`, `tree/Base/Console.h`, `tree/glue/provenance.cpp` | FerriteCAD's build glue | MIT |
| `PROVENANCE.txt` | the release, its checked digest and the compiler that built this | MIT |
| `REPLACING.md` | this file | MIT |

**The glue is FerriteCAD's, not FreeCAD's.** Four small files are written by
this project so planegcs builds outside FreeCAD: an export macro, an empty
build-configuration header, a silent console, and the function that returns
the provenance string. They are MIT and say so in their first lines. Nothing
under `tree/App/planegcs/` is touched.

## Provenance

- source: FreeCAD @TAG@, `src/Mod/Sketcher/App/planegcs`
- archive: `@ARCHIVE_URL@`
- archive SHA-256: `@SHA256@`, verified before anything was extracted
- built on: @PLATFORM@ with @COMPILER@
- the library answers `@PROVENANCE@` when asked what it is

## Replacing it

planegcs is linked dynamically for exactly this reason. Nothing of it is
compiled into a FerriteCAD binary, so you can put your own build in its place
without rebuilding anything of FerriteCAD's.

Rebuild from the source beside this file:

```
cmake -S <ferritecad>/tools/planegcs -B build \
  -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
  -DFCAD_PLANEGCS_TREE=$PWD/tree \
  -DFCAD_EIGEN_INCLUDE=<dir containing Eigen/> \
  -DFCAD_BOOST_INCLUDE=<dir containing boost/> \
  -DFCAD_PLANEGCS_PROVENANCE='@PROVENANCE@'
cmake --build build --config Release
```

Or build it any other way you like, from these sources or from a newer
planegcs. What has to hold is the file name and the C++ interface:

- the file must be called `@LIBRARY@` and sit where this one sits;
- it must export the `GCS::` classes declared in `tree/App/planegcs/GCS.h`,
  `Geo.h` and `Constraints.h`, compiled by a toolchain that agrees with
  FerriteCAD's about the C++ ABI and the C runtime;
- on Windows it must also produce `@IMPORT_LIBRARY@`, which is what a relink
  reads;
- it must export `fc_planegcs_provenance()` returning a string that says which
  planegcs it is. `tree/glue/provenance.cpp` is that function; compile it in.
  Nothing loads a library that cannot answer, which is deliberate: it is what
  stops a swapped library from going unnoticed.

Then relink or rerun:

```
FCAD_PLANEGCS_DIR=<this directory> cargo test -p ferritecad-solver-lab \
  --features planegcs -- --nocapture
```

Eigen and Boost are needed as headers only, at build time, and are not part of
this delivery. Eigen is MPL-2.0 and Boost is under the Boost Software Licence.

## What this delivery is not

A FerriteCAD release. Nothing in the FerriteCAD application loads planegcs
today. This is the component and the bench that measures it, packaged with the
obligations that would apply if it were shipped, so that the obligations are
tested rather than promised.
